{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/921890-dresden-files-as-mtaw-game","id":921890,"title":"Dresden Files as MtAw game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-27T01:12:28-07:00","id":921890,"title":"Dresden Files as MtAw game","content":"In new corebook, <b>Dresden Files</b> series is mentioned ( next to <b>Constatine</b> ) as main mages related inspiration. So let\u2019s dissect stories and character for ideas on <b>Mage</b> game and <b>CoD</b> on general. Just let\u2019s stick outside of outright spoilers \u2013 describing elements from particular book is okay \u2013 saying what happened to characters is not.<br /> <br /> I know that Dresden\u2019s magic is based on emotions, not secret truths like one of Awakened \u2013 but similarities are more profound when you look over details. Here are some of them.<ul><li><b>High Speech and Dresden\u2019s \u2018Babble Incantations\u2019</b> \u2013 Even when used from different reasons ( Dresden do this to separates him from power, in Mage it\u2019s \u2018blueprint of universe\u2019 ), end effect is the same \u2013 magic use is babbling to Sleepers ear. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/900642-2e-option-high-speech-variants\">Awakened can even go with Dresden\u2019s way of incanting random words from foreign languages</a>. 8-)</li> </ul><ul><li><b>Yantras/Instruments and Dresden\u2019s Props </b>\u2013 They really sound as the same. Just see Wikia description of Props in Dresdenverse:</li> </ul><i>\u2018<b>Props</b></i><br /> <i>Most magical practitioners use various props (physical objects) in the casting of their spells. It isn't actually necessary to do so. Any spell can be cast as an entirely mental construct, but the more complex a spell is, the more the practitioner has to divide his or her concentration.</i><br /> <i>Using props reduces the amount of mental effort needed to cast a spell by providing a visible object which encapsulates the meaning that the practitioner assigns to it. In other words, a prop is a symbolic placeholder for a part of the spell in the practitioner's mind.\u2018</i><br /> <br /> Sounds a lot like <b>Awakening</b>\u2019s Yantras, don\u2019t it?<ul><li><b>Consilium and <a href=\"http://dresdenfiles.wikia.com/wiki/White_Council\" target=\"_blank\">White Council</a></b> \u2013 On local level, they seem the same, i.e. Chicago\u2019s White Council looks just like Consilium system \u2013 even Wardens works just as Sentinels in <b>Mage</b>. Difference is on the world wide level \u2013 but I could argue that World Wide Council looks like Global Convocations that Silver Ladder tries to enact from forever.</li> </ul><ul><li><b>Quiescence </b>\u2013 This effect is not called in Dresdenverse, but comic\u2019s Welcome to the Jungle panel looks like best definition of phenomena for <b>Mage</b>:</li> </ul><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/813286-2ed-lie-dissonance-and-quiescence#post813286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (...) just after Harry Dresden acknowledges that the he used magic to the Sleeper's face\u2026<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/bYmYjft.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/bYmYjft.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T01:28:41-07:00","id":921895,"title":"","content":"Now to the main characters from <i>Storm Front</i> in <b>Dresden Files </b>as they would be in <b>Mage</b>:<ul><li><b>Harry Dresden</b> \u2013 Obrimos Adamantine Arrow private investigator with chivalric bent. His Long Term Nimbus is corrupting electronics.</li> </ul><ul><li><b>\u2018Bob\u2019</b> \u2013 Harry\u2019s Familiar, anchored to scull in his Sanctum. He is with formidable power, so he is rather powerful ( as <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917247-2e-optional-advanced-mage-merits\">Rank 3 Familiar being</a> ). In books he is Air Spirit with Influences in Knowledge. In TV series, he is fellow Ghost Mage.</li> </ul><ul><li><b>Donald Morgan </b>\u2013 Chicago\u2019s Sentinel of local Consilium. Using his position as punishing tool sounds like <i>Lex Magica </i>Merit of Silver Ladder, even if character looks more as Adamantine Arrow. Still I cannot guess his Path\u2026</li> </ul><ul><li><b>Karrin Murphy \u2013 </b>Mortal hunter that leads police \u2018Special Investigations\u2019 Devision. Interesting is that most of her subordinates do not acknowledge supernatural, so they are not hunters, only normal Sleepers. Case can be made that Murphy would be Sleepwalker.</li> </ul><ul><li><b>Susan Rodrigez </b>\u2013 Second mortal hunter, this time coming from journalist career, working for new age tabloid. Clearly Sleepwalker.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T07:16:00-07:00","id":921989,"title":"","content":"Remember that anyone with 1 dot of Status in Silver Ladder can take Lex Magica. Morgan can easily be an Adamantine Arrow person with 1 dot of Ladder, and a lot of Consilium Status; Lex Magica uses higher of the two between Consilium and Ladder Status.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T11:03:43-07:00","id":922099,"title":"","content":"I'm curious, why did you choose Adamantine Arrow for Dresden's Order? I've only just started listening to the series on audiobook, so I don't know enough to say with confidence one way or the other, but so far Dresden doesn't really strike me as particularly motivated to seek out conflict or challenge himself for its own sake. Is there something I might not know about yet being only a short way into the first book that marks him as a good fit for the Arrows?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T11:11:16-07:00","id":922100,"title":"","content":"I've only finished first book, but he seemed to me like an Apostate PC, who is disillusioned with flaws of all orders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T11:50:15-07:00","id":922129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/921890-dresden-files-as-mtaw-game?p=922099#post922099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious, why did you choose Adamantine Arrow for Dresden's Order?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was mentioned few times by <b>DaveB</b>...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/582780-awakening-second-edition-the-adamantine-arrow?p=584724#post584724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Harry is completely an Arrow. Within the variations for living in a universe that's not set up the same as the World of Darkness, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>My quick search also lead me to interesting conversation about Dresdenverse factions at large...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/502098-open-development-supporting-cast?p=503404#post503404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For those who are familiar with the Dresden Files, and I'm certain Dave and the Mage crew are fans since Harry Dresden is often an example of various Mage archetypes and issues (e.g., Harry is the quintessential low-Wisdom, yet &quot;good,&quot; wizard), do you see the increased parallels with the DF universe now that sleepers and all manner of sleepwalkers and minor talents are tied to the inherent social fabric of the Mage setting?<br /> <br /> In the Dresden Files, there are numerous supernaturally talented and informed human individuals and groups (and ample other supernatural bengs), but the White Council of Wizards are the veritable top of the magic food chain, who are responsible for keeping a lid on all the big magical cr@p in the setting, but are also terrifying to those whom they counsel and protect (usually because they have a habit of executing anyone alleged to broken the Rules and Magic, and due process and mercy are not priorities). In Mage 2e, particularly with their large and growing number of major and minor templates and various antagonists, I see the supernal mages of the Pentacle and Seers as the type of scary powerful people whom the nWOD mediums, psychokinetics, clairvoyants, dabblers in static magic and others, go to for help and protection or seeking power and knowledge, but otherwise know to stay the hell out of their way for their own safety, and make damn sure no true mage finds them in any way &quot;mysterious.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/502098-open-development-supporting-cast?p=503421#post503421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah - as Harry is to the inhabitants of Mac's pub, an Adamantine Arrow mage is to assorted occultists.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>What I exceptionally\u200b strike for Harry as Arrow is that Arrows can take Oaths as their Obsessions</b> - basicly the missions to fullfil that grants Arcane Beats. Dresden is chivalry wizard that practition magic by helping others with they supernatural problems - if this is not Arrow archetype, I do not know what Arrows are then.<br /> <br /> And let's not forget of his magic - <a href=\"http://dresdenfiles.wikia.com/wiki/Harry_Dresden#Magic\" target=\"_blank\">Dresden Wikia on Harry's subject</a>:<br /> <br /> <i>As one of the most powerful younger wizards of the White Council, Harry has a large repertoire of magical powers. His skills at evocation, or \u2018quick and dirty\u2019 magic, aka &quot;kaboom magic&quot;, aka &quot;battle magic&quot;, lean toward large blasts of fire and force, sometimes using wind, and also has some skill with earth (usually manipulating gravity) and lightning magic. He has considerable magical brute strength, though his control is initially somewhat lacking - for example, while he could easily shatter a pair of handcuffs, he may also break the wrists of the person wearing them. For this reason, Harry is ofttimes referred to as a magical 'thug'. Later in the series, Harry is also shown to have tremendous power in ritual form battle magic, when he uses the energy of a ley line to concentrate gravity for several miles around into a small zone, and flattens hundreds of enemy combatants at once.</i><br /> <br /> And his Dedicated Magial Tool - <a href=\"http://dresdenfiles.wikia.com/wiki/Staff_(focus)\" target=\"_blank\">Staff</a> <i>\u2014 A long staff used for channeling magic. Also works well as a bludgeoning weapon. </i>In TV series, it changed to hockey stick, that looks for me as even more Arrow move. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> His other favorite magical item - <a href=\"http://dresdenfiles.wikia.com/wiki/Shield_bracelet\" target=\"_blank\">Shield bracelet</a> <i>\u2014 A bracelet with tiny medieval shield charms on it. Used for creating force fields. The bracelet began as a simple silver construction, but has evolved to feature a chain of multiple metals woven together and shields of different metals. </i><br /> <br /> <b>Yeah, Harry is Arrow mage - Maybe less 'warrior' but more 'detective', but still Arrow in the heart.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Add-On:</b> There is also one thought that <b>DaveB</b> pointed in Open Development phase on Harry...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/303784-magical-self-defence-is-it-realistically-possible?p=308153#post308153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you drop off the end completely and become a Mad One (and how I dislike the name for them, for the wrong connotations it gives. Still, it's better than &quot;Maurauder&quot;) I don't see low Wisdom as a <i>punishment</i>, more a reflection of how you're playing your character. If the character imagos first and thinks second, no matter how good his intentions, he should be low Wisdom.<br /> <br /> Which is where my partially-quoted &quot;Harry Dresden is Wisdom 3&quot; comes from. Not a statement of fact - that'd be ludicrous, as he's a character from a different world who has his own roleplaying game - but a mission statement for myself and David Hill, who wrote Wisdom fresh from Humanity and Harmony. The corollory, of course, is that you can be an utter asshole and have Wisdom 10. Precise Evil is still evil, but your relative nice-ness is not something I want Wisdom to model.</div> </div> </div> </div>Harry is example of 'Good Intentions, Low Wisdom' by design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-27-2016, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T13:38:38-07:00","id":922192,"title":"","content":"Cool, thanks for the analysis! I can definitely see why Adamantine Arrow is a good fit for him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T13:55:24-07:00","id":922202,"title":"","content":"Harry is so Arrow it hurts.<br /> <br /> I would argue he's not so low as some people suggest. Certainly not high, but I would argue he's around 5 to 7. Obtaining Wisdom a nigh-on perpetual Obsession of his, particularly as he realizes more and more of the consequences of his actions. Harry's always questioning the impact of his actions, and if he's not, he's often learning them regardless. So he's stuck in this tug-of-war act where he' often does acts that cause his Wisdom to drop, and yet spends much of his time building it right back up.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Thought experiment for point of comparison: If Marcone were a mage, he'd probably be a high Wisdom mage-not because he's good, hell no. Ethical in his own way, yes, but mainly, Marcone is a <i>precise</i> individual. As a general rule, Marcone has what he wants executed with exactness, and when it doesn't pan out nicely, there's hell to pay. That exacting nature, if he had magic, would strongly mean it was his will, not his nature, that determines the course of his magic, which is pretty much Wisdom in a nutshell.<br /> <br /> Dresden loses and regains, Marcone just keeps it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-27-2016, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T14:01:55-07:00","id":922206,"title":"","content":"It must be noted: While none of his morals, ethics, or behaviors really falls that far in line with them, Dresden's tendency to watch the White Council with wariness, particularly as far as weeding out the Black Council goes, does give him some Guardian-like qualities, as befits an operative in the Grey Council. He's still Arrow as shit, and Ebenezar is really the one you'd have to pin the Guardian title on, but it's worth noting nonetheless. In Awakening terms, Dresden might not like the Guardians, but he'd be in a weird place where he'd honestly trust them more than anyone else, and while he might need some pushing, he'd probably work with them more than the thearchs and mystagogues.<br /> <br /> That said, Dresden loves him some libertines, apostates, heretics, and nameless orders, and as has been stated, he'd probably honestly be a Nameless Solitaire if he felt it was worth it. EDIT: And in fairness, Morgan was, in ways, more Guardian than Arrow, and that should tell you more on that mixed feeling Dresden works with.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually Morgan as a thearch enforcer makes a lot of sense. Also, I would argue Bob is at least Rank 4, possibly 5. Evil Bob's various incursions has shown off how damn powerful Bob is.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Finally read Wyrd's full explanation of Dresden as an Awakening character, particularly as an Arrow. Well done!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-27-2016, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T16:52:13-07:00","id":922294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/921890-dresden-files-as-mtaw-game?p=922099#post922099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious, why did you choose Adamantine Arrow for Dresden's Order? I've only just started listening to the series on audiobook, so I don't know enough to say with confidence one way or the other, but so far Dresden doesn't really strike me as particularly motivated to seek out conflict or challenge himself for its own sake. Is there something I might not know about yet being only a short way into the first book that marks him as a good fit for the Arrows?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes there is stuff later on that would push him towards fitting with the Arrows, but I still agree with your assessment. He's not interested in conflict or challenge at all. In fact he hates it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/921890-dresden-files-as-mtaw-game?p=922202#post922202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Harry is so Arrow it hurts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree. Harry's driving passions that fuel his fire magic are both his belief that the strong should never harm the weak, and his love for magic as a creative art form. Harry explains at one point how he most enjoys sitting next to his fireplace reading a good book with his pets, and doing magical experiments in his lab. He says that if that were his whole life, he would be content and satisfied. However, he nevertheless accepts the call to adventure because of his desire to safeguard the weak. Ultimately, Harry strives for peace. He may seek out conflict in the end, but he doesn't do it for conflict's sake.<br /> <br /> He doesn't believe in conflict as a virtue to be exalted, but as an unfortunate necessity that in a perfect world would be better-off eliminated. You can see this most in his views on how apprentices should be trained in shielding magic. He was trained by having baseballs thrown at him by his mentor. He rejects that idea as cruel and immoral and refuses to repeat the practice. Arrow philosophy would disagree entirely with this decision.<br /> <br /> You can see how he hates conflict when he withholds information from those around him to keep them from getting involved. An Arrow would be supportive of others who want to seek out conflict and become stronger. Harry is the opposite. Remember how he says &quot;Chivalry is not dead&quot;? He sees weakness and naivety as a virtue to be protected, not a flaw to be outgrown. He hopes that by taking the whole conflict on himself, he can prevent others from having to suffer as well. He would rather others remain weak and peaceful, than to allow them to suffer the conflict he hates so much - even if it means his undoing.<br /> <br /> He might fit in enough to be a member, but he'd promote heretical views. Ultimately he rejects the Arrows' core tenet that conflict is magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 06-27-2016, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T17:25:05-07:00","id":922309,"title":"","content":"I think it's not unfair to say it's a subject he wrestles with. He just as often points out that life is struggle and conflict, an unavoidable human condition, but believes that the conflict improves and hones humanity-but as you say, on the other hand he doesn't believe everyone should. But he very definitely takes it on himself.<br /> <br /> It might be more accurate to say that the standards he holds for himself are very Arrow-esque, in a lot of ways, even as he doesn't want to personally engage in conflict constantly, but more importantly he differs from his fellows in that he doesn't believe his standards apply to others(and in fact, both sides of that argument get argued with him on several different fronts and different directions).<br /> <br /> But more importantly, you are right. Ultimately, Dresden's not really an Order mage, even really a Nameless Order. He's benefitted from them over time, and he has a mixed, if leaning positive, opinion of them, but if the Wardens hadn't basically leveraged the circumstances, a list of freedoms, and his conscience against him, he'd've never joined his worlds' version of the Arrows(/Guardians/thearch enforcers). He <i>does</i> have a very Arrow mentality though. It need not be perfect on all fronts for him to still have that, and where he aligns with them(which is a lot beyond the central tenet of conflict), he believes <i>deeply</i>, to a point of hurting.<br /> <br /> But in the end, he is Nameless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T17:47:49-07:00","id":922319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/921890-dresden-files-as-mtaw-game?p=921895#post921895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2018Bob\u2019 \u2013 Harry\u2019s Familiar, anchored to scull in his Sanctum. He is with formidable power, so he is rather powerful ( as <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917247-2e-optional-advanced-mage-merits\">Rank 3 Familiar being</a> ). In books he is Air Spirit with Influences in Knowledge. In TV series, he is fellow Ghost Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not clear whether Bob would still be an Air spirit in the Mage universe. Dresden calls him an Air spirit because Air is the classical element of analysis, logic, wisdom, and understanding. It's not entirely clear whether Air is truly Bob's nature, or just Harry's understanding of Bob.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 06-27-2016, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T19:23:53-07:00","id":922369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/921890-dresden-files-as-mtaw-game?p=922319#post922319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not clear whether Bob would still be an Air spirit in the Mage universe. Dresden calls him an Air spirit because Air is the classical element of analysis, logic, wisdom, and understanding. It's not entirely clear whether Air is truly Bob's nature, or just Harry's understanding of Bob.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've come to understand the air as being incidental to Bob's nature as a spirit of intellect, a product of him being a classical spirit. He's primarily identified as intellect, and yet even as of late his power in exercise is in air as a medium for his nature.<br /> <br /> In ChroD terms, the concept he was born out of either has permissible room for him to have devoured Air Spirit motes or the design of mages will for him to have it as Influence and relevant numina without derailing him, or he's one of the least egregious magath out there.<br /> <br /> Now, mind you, and muddling the affair, this is assuming he's not actually a Goetic equivalent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T20:27:31-07:00","id":922404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/921890-dresden-files-as-mtaw-game?p=922369#post922369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've come to understand the air as being incidental to Bob's nature as a spirit of intellect, a product of him being a classical spirit. He's primarily identified as intellect, and yet even as of late his power in exercise is<span style=\"font-family:arial\"> in air as a medium</span> for his nature.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">In ChroD terms, the concept he was born out of either has permissible room for him to have devoured Air Spirit motes or the design of mages will for him to have it as Influence and relevant numina without derailing him, or he's one of the least egregious magath out there.<br /> <br /> Now, mind you, and muddling the affair, this is assuming he's not actually a Goetic equivalent.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The classical element of air is associated with two major properties: &quot;Moistness&quot; and &quot;Warmth&quot; (think breath, not wind). Moistness represents formlessness; the ability to adapt and conform due to lack of strict shape and rigid structure. Warmth is the power of separation, which breaks apart mixed things and causes them to attract others of their kind, so that they become sorted by type (as with an alembic or an </span></span><a href=\"http://chemistry.elmhurst.edu/vchembook/images/513refine.JPEG\" target=\"_blank\">oil distillation tower</a><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">). When you combine the two, you get that air is the element of formless intangible things, and has the ability to sort them into their component parts...or in other words, air is the element of analysis. Breaking intangible ideas and concepts down to understand them. Hence why Bob is described interchangeably as a spirit of air and a spirit of intellect.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T01:19:39-07:00","id":922500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/921890-dresden-files-as-mtaw-game?p=922294#post922294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes there is stuff later on that would push him towards fitting with the Arrows, but I still agree with your assessment. He's not interested in conflict or challenge at all. In fact he hates it<br /> <br /> (...)<br /> <br /> You can see how he hates conflict when he withholds information from those around him to keep them from getting involved. An Arrow would be supportive of others who want to seek out conflict and become stronger. Harry is the opposite. Remember how he says &quot;Chivalry is not dead&quot;? He sees weakness and naivety as a virtue to be protected, not a flaw to be outgrown. He hopes that by taking the whole conflict on himself, he can prevent others from having to suffer as well. He would rather others remain weak and peaceful, than to allow them to suffer the conflict he hates so much - even if it means his undoing.<br /> <br /> He might fit in enough to be a member, but he'd promote heretical views. Ultimately he rejects the Arrows' core tenet that conflict is magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Harry is Arrow - he is just Vidantus from start ( I.e. Pacifistic Arrow ). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AA, p.66</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Vidanti</b><br /> The Adamantine Arrow has rituals for members who lose their fighting spirit. They become the Vidanti (\u201cthose who are to be shunned\u201d). The specifics vary from culture to culture. The following example hails from 16th -century England and is still used, though the language has changed with time.<br /> A Vidantus is no longer a member of the order. Furthermore, she vows not to join any order, and not work against the Diamond orders. Arrows should shun Vidanti so that they will not join the Vidanti\u2019s dishonor or despair. Most importantly, a Vidantus cannot, under any circumstances, counsel any Arrow to follow the Vidantus\u2019s path. Vidantus status is irreversible. If a mage wants to change her mind, she\u2019s failed both the order and her own moral resolve and is a useless person.<br /> Despite these steep restrictions, Vidanti are actually quite common. In some regions, it\u2019s traditional for aged or severely injured Arrows to turn Vidantus. They often have their own cloisters and societies. Other caucuses<br /> levy Vidantus as punishment for cowardice. But most often, Arrows become Vidanti because their ability to fight has been seared away by traumatic experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Harry believes in nobler parts of Arrows tents - but do not believe that violence is necessary. He still will self-defense himself or those important to him. It's Vidantus written all over it. It also answer why he is a bit outsider in wizards society. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-28-2016, 04:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T16:42:38-07:00","id":922912,"title":"","content":"Pacifist, Harry ain't. Harry's never been a pacifist.<br /> <br /> And again, all violence is conflict but not all conflict is violence, barring loose definitions of violence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T18:47:12-07:00","id":922971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/921890-dresden-files-as-mtaw-game?p=922294#post922294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snip for space.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought this thread would have moved too far by now for me to make a relevant post, but I agree with this 100%. Harry just wants to be Wizard Joe Schmoe. Just a random guy tinkering around with magic and exploring it's possibilities while waxing poetic about it for hours at anyone who asks him about it. He likes stability, doesn't like change, doesn't like attention or threatening people or bossing them around. He just wants to do research and be left alone.<br /> <br /> It is unfortunate, then, that his GM has decided to turn him in to the wizard equivalent of the terminator by throwing circumstance and coincidence his way until he becomes better at blowing stuff up than puzzling things out (okay, it's good at both, but <i>really</i> good at blowing shit up).<br /> <br /> I'd peg him as a Mysterium who just wants to be left alone and learn, but the universe loves to watch him suffer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T19:42:08-07:00","id":923000,"title":"","content":"THe Mysterium's disdain for Sleepers is ridiculously counter to Dresden's mindset, as is their bureaucracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T23:22:57-07:00","id":923109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/921890-dresden-files-as-mtaw-game?p=922912#post922912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pacifist, Harry ain't. Harry's never been a pacifist.<br /> <br /> And again, all violence is conflict but not all conflict is violence, barring loose definitions of violence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being Vidanti does not mean you are 'all the time pacifist' - rather you <i>strive</i> for world where you do not need to fight. But Vidanti, being previous full Arrows, still can self-defense or casting combat magic in important moments - <i>they just do not like to do it</i>. Which is Harry, at least till the end of second book as I listen to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T07:06:43-07:00","id":923227,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's because I'm up to Changes in the series, but I don't see Harry as a Vidanti. He's constantly throwing down challenges to bad guys and rivals. Heck, he gets more prone to challenge people head-to-head as the series goes on.<br /> <br /> The below will contain spoilers up to Changes, so be warned. <br /> <br /> Harry is definitely an Obrimos- his go-to spells are wind and fire, with some lightning thrown in as conditions allow. His stunt with Sue bespeaks either insane luck or some talent with Death, aided by the necromantic energies being gathered for the Darkhollow and the fact that there was a convenient leyline. <br /> <br /> Molly is a Mastigos who started out with major talent in Mind, but the White Council's prohibition on tampering with other's minds led Harry to coach her in other Arcana, particularly Forces, to the point that she can essentially become a one-woman rave through the creation of lights and sounds. <br /> <br /> Carlos shows off a lot of water magic, which is Matter. Luccio could be an Obrimos, what with that laser-beam-of-white-hot-fire spell in Dead Beat. Rashid, being the Gatekeeper, shows a lot of talent with Space, but his true power seems to rest with Time; the dude definitely has pretty high Wisdom, seeing as how he knows exactly how to get people to act without altering the future without changing things too drastically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 06-29-2016, 11:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T09:24:56-07:00","id":925377,"title":"","content":"I'm current with the series, so I will try to offer opinions without spoilers:<br /> <br /> I'm on board with Harry being Obrimos / Arrow. He definitely started out as Apostate, just trying to stay below the Council's radar and not get in any more trouble. Basically he ended up getting forced to choose and the only choice available to him was Arrow. He still would prefer to not -have- to fight. He has reiterated on multiple occasions that his joy is magic itself - just studying it and experimenting with it for its own sake - but when push comes to shove, Chicago is HIS city and he WILL defend it from all comers using every tool in his vast magical arsenal.<br /> <br /> What I'm -not- sure how to reconcile via Mage or other Chronicles rule-sets is the more recent stuff (from Changes to present) regarding Mab and the choice he makes there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12034-jmkoontz1980","name":"jmkoontz1980","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T09:47:31-07:00","id":925388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jmkoontz1980</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/921890-dresden-files-as-mtaw-game?p=925377#post925377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm -not- sure how to reconcile via Mage or other Chronicles rule-sets is the more recent stuff (from Changes to present) regarding Mab and the choice he makes there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it's simple.<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">He developed a new Prelacy.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T09:54:27-07:00","id":925390,"title":"","content":"Or a legacy based around an alliance with Winter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T10:33:13-07:00","id":925403,"title":"","content":"But both of those rely on it being an Awakened in his position. I'm pretty sure the guy before him was not Awakened, so what sort of catch-all option is there to add that on top of whatever other Template someone might already have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12034-jmkoontz1980","name":"jmkoontz1980","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T12:08:26-07:00","id":925450,"title":"","content":"Oh, duh, it's a Pact from Summoners.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T23:31:31-07:00","id":925756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/921890-dresden-files-as-mtaw-game?p=925450#post925450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, duh, it's a Pact from Summoners.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can only point out that you can make Legacy bases on Pact - that you are first member and creator. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T10:40:08-07:00","id":925970,"title":"","content":"Sleepwalkers can't join legacies though and typically that's what the Knights of the Fae Courts are. A Pact of Vassalage makes more sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T08:02:39-07:00","id":928135,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the more I thought about it, the more I was thinking either this or a really strong Pledge from Changeling","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12034-jmkoontz1980","name":"jmkoontz1980","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T08:07:42-07:00","id":929744,"title":"","content":"Perhaps Mab has access to Beast kinship abilities on steroids. Mechanically it's a bit clumsy but many, many, many templates in Dresden are described as taking on a sort of second set of hungers attached to the power that constantly push and scratch away at a person's sense of self.<br /> <br /> That being said, sufficiently willful beings can maintain more than one mantle which runs counter to COFD's one template only policy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1881,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1881-the-cowardly-scion","user":"The Cowardly Scion","date":". 07-11-2016, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1881-the-cowardly-scion","name":"The Cowardly Scion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1881_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T19:08:04-07:00","id":930107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cowardly Scion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/921890-dresden-files-as-mtaw-game?p=929744#post929744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps Mab has access to Beast kinship abilities on steroids. Mechanically it's a bit clumsy but many, many, many templates in Dresden are described as taking on a sort of second set of hungers attached to the power that constantly push and scratch away at a person's sense of self.<br /> <br /> That being said, sufficiently willful beings can maintain more than one mantle which runs counter to COFD's one template only policy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that any Sidhe met in the series is either a True Fae or hobgoblin. The changelings of Dresden Files aren't a one-to-one for the CoD changelings, but oh well. The Knights could be Fae-touched from Changeling 2e. The Ladies are True Fae are on the low end of the power scale. The Queens are about as powerful as True Fae can get, while the Mothers are pretty much goddesses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T19:33:34-07:00","id":930122,"title":"","content":"Eh, if you're trying to relate it in purely Mage terms though there's no need to to crossover into other game lines. Come up with Bound or Supernal/Astral/Underworld//Spirit/Cryptid/Lower Depths type patrons as needs demand.<br /> <br /> Mab could as easily be a highly influential Fate primary Supernal entity as anything else. Probably has Death as a secondary arcana to explain the cold and a few other things.<br /> <br /> I mean yeah, you can go to crossover if you're comfortable with it, but Mage has a lot going on in house too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T07:31:55-07:00","id":939519,"title":"","content":"The mantle of the knight could be itself an entity. I'm sure one of the claiming/posessing/riding/whatevs conditions can fit the relationship. If not, conditions are meant to be altered and created to fit the narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T21:50:40-08:00","id":1021474,"title":"","content":"Listening to <i>Summer Knight </i>now and I think that <i><b>Mab</b></i> works great as <b>Changeling</b>'s Queen of Winter Court with high Wyrd . She is not <i>enough</i> predatory to be True Fae snatching people ( at least to my knowledge ) for making more changelings, but she is 'cold' enough to be <b>CoD</b> Winter Courtier. Only that she is more <u>creating</u> Sorrow by her plans, than just meeting people in it for Glamour, like on random funerals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T22:19:47-08:00","id":1021477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/921890-dresden-files-as-mtaw-game?p=1021474#post1021474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Listening to <i>Summer Knight </i>now and I think that <i><b>Mab</b></i> works great as <b>Changeling</b>'s Queen of Winter Court with high Wyrd . She is not <i>enough</i> predatory to be True Fae snatching people ( at least to my knowledge ) for making more changelings, but she is 'cold' enough to be <b>CoD</b> Winter Courtier. Only that she is more <u>creating</u> Sorrow by her plans, than just meeting people in it for Glamour, like on random funerals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes creating the emotion you feed on is one of the best ways to keep yourself full. It's why I believe when folks only think changelings are passive feeders, it annoys me. Yes you can do it, but you're basically on a diet, and can't use your powers as much as a more active harvester. To be more powerful more often, you got to be a bigger manipulator more often. The mechanics are encouraging the player to make the emotions they need to feed. Sorrow Fear Anger Happiness. A changeling can wait all night at a bar for a brawl and get one feed in. But a changeling that bar hops around the city and actively starts fights can get a couple of good feeds in. The grim tales are all about the fae generally dicking with people.<br /> <br /> So the next time you need sorrow don't be afraid of tracking down the family dog and letting an 'accident' happen. That's the monstrous of changeling. Breaking the stability of normal folks lives so you can power your abilities just a little longer<br /> <br /> The series is also great for the amount of adhering to the Letter of the Law and not he spirit. Which is changeling wordplay and it is amazing.<br /> <br /> Creating elaborate schemes to collect glamor en mass is great plot fodder. And do Enjoy the book I know I have","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":11731,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","user":"MercSet","date":".  spelling 12-24-2016, 01:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T06:23:29-08:00","id":1024736,"title":"","content":"Listening to more <i>Summer Knight</i> I see they have interesting Court dynamics. There are three Queens for each - Mother, proper Queen and Lady. Queen is now ruling, Mother is previous ruling and Lady is coming to rule next. Could be fun to run this in <b>Changeling</b> with Queen having Mantle 5, Mother 5+ as 'Queen Emeritus' and Lady being Mantle 4 'Queen to be'.<br /> <br /> Also, am I right, or does Dresdenverse Courts are having hobgoblin in their Courts ranks? Like <a href=\"http://dresdenfiles.wikia.com/wiki/Toot-Toot\" target=\"_blank\">Toot-Toot </a>seems much more hobgoblin to me than proper changeling. Also, generally <a href=\"http://dresdenfiles.wikia.com/wiki/Wyldfae\" target=\"_blank\">Wyldfae</a> sounds like they would be hobgoblins in <b>Changeling</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T06:59:26-08:00","id":1024743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/921890-dresden-files-as-mtaw-game?p=1024736#post1024736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Listening to more <i>Summer Knight</i> I see they have interesting Court dynamics. There are three Queens for each - Mother, proper Queen and Lady. Queen is now ruling, Mother is previous ruling and Lady is coming to rule next. Could be fun to run this in <b>Changeling</b> with Queen having Mantle 5, Mother 5+ as 'Queen Emeritus' and Lady being Mantle 4 'Queen to be'.<br /> <br /> Also, am I right, or does Dresdenverse Courts are having hobgoblin in their Courts ranks? Like <a href=\"http://dresdenfiles.wikia.com/wiki/Toot-Toot\" target=\"_blank\">Toot-Toot </a>seems much more hobgoblin to me than proper changeling. Also, generally <a href=\"http://dresdenfiles.wikia.com/wiki/Wyldfae\" target=\"_blank\">Wyldfae</a> sounds like they would be hobgoblins in <b>Changeling</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorta. Except that the Mothers are <b>much </b>more cosmically significant and magically powerful than the mere title of &quot;previous queens&quot; would imply. In Changeling terms, the Mothers are more akin to True Fae.<br /> <br /> But then again, the fae of the Dresden Files do not work at all like those of Changeling, so it's hard to draw a comparison. Wyldfae could be hobgoblins, but then we have the Kings of Summer and Winter who are both Wyldfae and Summer/Winter Fae respectively. They also seems to rival the Queens in magical power, although of lower authority. So they probably aren't hobgoblins at all, but some sort of high-Wyrd changelings or once again True Fae themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T07:05:29-08:00","id":1024745,"title":"","content":"So what should we consider the Knights of the Cross?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T08:53:09-08:00","id":1024775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/921890-dresden-files-as-mtaw-game?p=1024745#post1024745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what should we consider the Knights of the Cross?</div> </div> </div> </div>As at 4th book, I would suspect Hunter Conspiracy, with Endowments not so different than CoD Malleus Maleficarum. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T09:01:38-08:00","id":1024777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/921890-dresden-files-as-mtaw-game?p=1024775#post1024775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As at 4th book, I would suspect Hunter Conspiracy, with Endowments not so different than CoD Malleus Maleficarum. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Conspiracy might be a little generous, there are of course only three of them. Unless we count the fact that they pretty have the entirety of the Catholic Church at their disposal for resources and supplies (one's Baptist and the other's agnostic, but we'll let that slide <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T18:36:32-08:00","id":1024963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/921890-dresden-files-as-mtaw-game?p=1024777#post1024777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Conspiracy might be a little generous, there are of course only three of them. Unless we count the fact that they pretty have the entirety of the Catholic Church at their disposal for resources and supplies (one's Baptist and the other's agnostic, but we'll let that slide <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they also have less material patrons that help them out. In that way, they'd be closer to the Cainite Heresy (at least regarding the Messengers).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T06:30:48-08:00","id":1025891,"title":"","content":"Ironiclly, <a href=\"http://dresdenfiles.wikia.com/wiki/Maeve\" target=\"_blank\">Maeve</a>, Lady of Winder in Dresdenverse, sounds as great inspiration for <b>CoD</b> Spring Queen. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T06:43:30-08:00","id":1025902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/921890-dresden-files-as-mtaw-game?p=1025891#post1025891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ironiclly, <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://dresdenfiles.wikia.com/wiki/Maeve&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Maeve</a>, Lady of Winder in Dresdenverse, sounds as great inspiration for <b>CoD</b> Spring Queen. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Maeve is a party animal but she's just as much about inflicting pain, misery and sorrow as anyone in Winter. Don't make the mistake of being fooled by the mask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T06:52:25-08:00","id":1025909,"title":"","content":"Ugh, how do I put spoiler tags again?<br /> <br /> Anyways, a spoiler for the Dresden Files regarding the fae Queens (drag over the text to see it):<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#ffffff\">Turns out Maeve the Winter Lady is a changeling (half-fae and half-human in the DF) who decided to become a fae. She has a sister, Sarissa, who decided to become human. And Mab the Winter Queen admits to Harry that she once used to be mortal. This probably holds true in extension to Titania the Summer Queen, and her daughter Aurora the Summer Lady.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T08:43:51-08:00","id":1026544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/921890-dresden-files-as-mtaw-game?p=1025909#post1025909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ugh, how do I put spoiler tags again?<br /> <br /> Anyways, a spoiler for the Dresden Files regarding the fae Queens (drag over the text to see it):</div> </div> </div> </div>You wrap the text in [ SPOILER ] [/ SPOILER ] tags (minus the spaces, of course).<br /> <br /> Like this:<br /> (Cold Days+ Spoiler)<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Remember, also, that Maeve was infected/corrupted by Outsider influence. Or, in Awakening's terms most likely, Abyssal.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T09:04:18-08:00","id":1026552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/921890-dresden-files-as-mtaw-game?p=1024743#post1024743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorta. Except that the Mothers are <b>much </b>more cosmically significant and magically powerful than the mere title of &quot;previous queens&quot; would imply. In Changeling terms, the Mothers are more akin to True Fae.<br /> <br /> But then again, the fae of the Dresden Files do not work at all like those of Changeling, so it's hard to draw a comparison. Wyldfae could be hobgoblins, but then we have the Kings of Summer and Winter who are both Wyldfae and Summer/Winter Fae respectively. They also seems to rival the Queens in magical power, although of lower authority. So they probably aren't hobgoblins at all, but some sort of high-Wyrd changelings or once again True Fae themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dresden spends more time with True Fae than changelings. Changelings and rough equivalents to them actually don't pop up all that much for him. Given his propensity for hanging out with smaller fish, this is actually quite notably weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T09:19:47-08:00","id":1026561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/921890-dresden-files-as-mtaw-game?p=1026552#post1026552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dresden spends more time with True Fae than changelings. Changelings and rough equivalents to them actually don't pop up all that much for him. Given his propensity for hanging out with smaller fish, this is actually quite notably weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, he was friends with a few Changelings. For a little bit, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T11:11:49-08:00","id":1026619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/921890-dresden-files-as-mtaw-game?p=1026552#post1026552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dresden spends more time with True Fae than changelings. Changelings and rough equivalents to them actually don't pop up all that much for him. Given his propensity for hanging out with smaller fish, this is actually quite notably weird.</div> </div> </div> </div> Define &quot;small fish.&quot; He has a few pure-mortal friends and the werewolf people. But if you look at who he rubs elbows with in the books? Faerie queens, an archangel, Knights of the Sword, influential members of the Inquisition, the ex-familar of the most powerful necromancer in history, Odin All-Father, a human mobster that is roughly a match just about any lesser supernatural faction, the ruler of the most populous vampire clan in the world and her brother.... I could go on. Dresden generally deals with the Powers That Be, not small fish. Even the pixie friends are pretty powerful. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T17:34:49-08:00","id":1026777,"title":"","content":"Considering Harry tends to make enemies with entities vastly powerful than him, being backed up by similarly powerful friends does good for him. Too bad his health and general well-being isn't being helped, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T03:20:20-08:00","id":1026952,"title":"","content":"I'm starting to be glad that I dropped the series in mid of book 2. Glancing through things people write about it it seems that it switched focus from &quot;detective stories using magical noir world as a setting&quot;to pretty standard (urban) fantasy stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T03:17:21-08:00","id":1028089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/921890-dresden-files-as-mtaw-game?p=1026952#post1026952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm starting to be glad that I dropped the series in mid of book 2. Glancing through things people write about it it seems that it switched focus from &quot;detective stories using magical noir world as a setting&quot;to pretty standard (urban) fantasy stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Missing out. There are still elements of detective work throughout them all, but the progression of opposition renders purely &quot;normal&quot; cases insufficient.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T09:55:36-08:00","id":1028195,"title":"","content":"Turn Coat was the best one, I felt they started dropping off after that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T04:44:47-08:00","id":1028499,"title":"","content":"The series generally still has that feel of occult detective thing, what with solving mysteries and intrigues. Yes, Harry gets stronger, enough to blast through most threats. But the threats he actually faces are almost always above his power level, so he still has to resort to doing it the 'smart' way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}